WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.375
Let’s run a DR track with a course change in it.

2
00:00:03.625 --> 00:00:05.475
Follow the diagram.

3
00:00:05.725 --> 00:00:10.450
You leave an eight hundred fix on course one two five true, at ten knots.

4
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:13.325
At nine hundred, plot a DR.

5
00:00:13.575 --> 00:00:17.975
One hour at ten knots puts it ten miles along one two five.

6
00:00:18.225 --> 00:00:20.625
At nine thirty you change course.

7
00:00:20.875 --> 00:00:24.075
A change of course means a DR at that moment.

8
00:00:24.325 --> 00:00:26.950
How far from the nine hundred DR?

9
00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:32.625
Half an hour at ten knots: five miles further along one two five.

10
00:00:32.875 --> 00:00:37.900
From that nine thirty DR, draw the new course line at one six zero true.

11
00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:41.975
At ten hundred, plot a DR five miles along it.

12
00:00:42.225 --> 00:00:45.150
And label every position with its time.

13
00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:49.150
If a fix comes in at any point, start a fresh track from it.
